Subject: Replay a cached add-transition store from compiled code before the frame is published

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_put_add` tries the site's cached add transition for a compiled named store: the
    same replay the interpreter's store handler does first. It returns 1 when the store landed,
    0 when the site holds no transition for the receiver's shape, and -1 when growing the
    property array failed.

Why we need it
  A constructor that sets its fields (`this.p = v`) takes the miss path of the inline store on
  every property, which published every live register to the frame before reaching the same
  replay. The replay only grows the property array, so nothing reads the registers.
  The replay needs no published registers: it neither starts a collection nor runs a finalizer
  (the realloc does not trigger one, and the pre-add shape it drops never holds the prototype's
  last reference because the cached new shape holds it too), so a value only in a C local
  stays valid.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -62407,6 +62407,23 @@
                : 0;
 }
 
+/* The cached add-transition store of a compiled named store, tried before the
+   frame is published: it only grows the property array, so nothing observes
+   the registers. 1 when the store landed, 0 when the site holds no transition
+   for the receiver's shape, -1 on exception. The value is borrowed.
+   Nothing here can start a collection or run a finalizer, so a value held only
+   in a C local stays valid: the realloc does not trigger one (only a new object
+   does), and the pre-add shape it drops is never the last holder of the
+   prototype, because the cached new shape holds the same one. */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_put_add(JSContext *ctx, JSRegRun *f, JSValue recv,
+                                 JSValue v, int site)
+{
+    if (f->pic == NULL || JS_VALUE_GET_TAG(recv) != JS_TAG_OBJECT)
+        return 0;
+    return regvm_put_field_add_hit(ctx, f->b, f->pic, JS_VALUE_GET_OBJ(recv),
+                                   v, site);
+}
+
 int qjs_aot_object_template_b(JSContext *ctx, JSFunctionBytecode *b, int index,
                              JSValue *out)
 {
